joe Linux: index and rindex, the old BSD names of strchr and strrchr, which glibc and musl keep,
and <string.h> including <strings.h> by default, as glibc's does; iproute2's tc calls index and
rindex with only <string.h>. On 32-bit Arm and x86 bionic already had index, for old NDK apps.

